From: Emmanuel <aloziefrompg@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 09:04:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Stop the live sheet from re-adding corrected emails as
 duplicates

The live sheet is only read by the dashboard, so correcting an email
here left the old address in the sheet. The next sync found nobody
with that address and added the guest a second time.

Corrections are now remembered per event (old address -> corrected
address). Every load of people (live sheet, CSV import, Supabase and
website forms) reads an old address as the corrected one, so it
updates the same guest. A sheet that holds both the wrong and the right
row becomes one guest.

For duplicates that already exist, Check emails shows the guest whose
corrected address is taken and offers Merge into <name>, one at a time
or all at once (owner only). The follow-up notes move to the kept
guest and the correction is remembered. A duplicate with a seat
reservation, ticket, check-in or payment is not merged automatically.

